{"nodes": [{"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_phase_state_ledger", "label": "Phase state \u2014 the append-only session ledger", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Appended at the end of every session per PRJ93_RULES.md; it is history, while BLOCKED_third_party.md \u00a7F is the state."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_prj93_rules", "label": "brain/PRJ93_RULES.md \u2014 the project ruleset", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Names the gates, the token discipline, the corrections-are-appended rule and the session lifecycle."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_overleaf_gate", "label": "Gate 5 \u2014 the Overleaf push is a human gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_graphify_hang", "label": "graphify query/explain appeared to hang", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Later contradicted: it returns a truncated subgraph in seconds and the apparent hang was a missing timeout binary on this shell. A null result from a guessed schema is not evidence of absence."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_phase_litconf", "label": "Phase LITCONF \u2014 literature conformance audit, six runs executed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gate 3 (rerun) was put and cleared for six runs; gate 1 was not taken, so TabPFN-TS remained open."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_notebooklm_is_a_search_index", "label": "NotebookLM is a search index, not an oracle", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wrong or NOT-IN-SOURCES on six claims that Zotero full text confirms verbatim, three sessions running; citation indices were scrambled in two of seven responses while the quoted text was correct."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_phase_8a_research_questions", "label": "Phase 8A \u2014 five research questions derived and approved", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The set maps one-to-one onto the five Results sections by design, so the trace is mechanical for a marker instead of an argument they must reconstruct."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_gap_limb_7_scoped_out", "label": "Gap limb 7 scoped out of the research questions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A stated question with no answer fails both trace criteria by construction, and HC59 already mandates the divergence appear in Discussion 5.5, so an RQ6 would state the same fact once where the rubric asks for it and once where it penalises it. Reversible in one direction only."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_unlock_trail", "label": "The unlock trail \u2014 U-rows for items reopened after approval", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A closed-approvals section edited without a trail stops being useful; this is the corrections-are-appended rule applied to approvals rather than findings."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_phase_8b_appendix_floats", "label": "Phase 8B \u2014 nine floats authored, programme closed to the compile", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_assertion_boundary", "label": "The assertion boundary \u2014 what a generator can and cannot verify", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Horizontal spans, overlap and origin placement are verified by generator assertion every run; vertical extent, overfull boxes and glyph collision only by the compile. When a fix moves an object, re-derive every constraint the object was subject to, not the one that prompted the move."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_proof_harness_false_answer", "label": "A proof that passes where the document fails", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "figure_proof.tex loaded algorithm2e alone, so three pages would have compiled clean while the document broke. Assert against the target, not the harness: the package block is part of the target's geometry."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_phase_8c1_chapter2", "label": "Phase 8C-1 \u2014 Chapter 2 recomposed and pushed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_chapter2_overrun_provisional", "label": "The Chapter 2 overrun is PROVISIONAL, not accepted", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An unmarked 22% overrun compounds: six chapters at that rate land the document at 24,400 against HC1's 20,000. Two derivations are tested for relocation before any cut is costed, so the residue is only irreducible once Methods' real floor is known."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_word_counter_defect", "label": "The word counter was defective \u2014 4,948, not 4,893", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stripping LaTeX comments with %.* also matches an escaped \\%, truncating every line quoting a percentage. The 'calibrated to 0.14%' claim is withdrawn because it compared a single aggregate against a single aggregate, which cannot detect a defect that moves both the same way."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_wordcount_py", "label": "brain/scripts/wordcount.py \u2014 the instrumented counter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Carries the per-chapter budgets, emits a paste-ready table with a delta, warns on tree divergence, and reports Raw / Artefact / Marker so equation-density over-reads cancel."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_instrumented_tool_rule", "label": "A number entering a decision comes from an instrumented tool with a fixture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two ad-hoc counters have now been wrong, both in the direction of the number about to be acted on, and both caught only by building the real tool and watching it disagree."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_withdrawal_propagation_rule", "label": "A withdrawal is retracted everywhere the claim was asserted", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The calibration claim was withdrawn in the ledger and left standing in wordcount.py's docstring, which is where the next reader would actually meet it."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_phase_8c2_chapter3", "label": "Phase 8C-2 \u2014 Chapter 3 recomposed, floor measured", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_chapter_boundary_check", "label": "The Chapter 2 / Chapter 3 boundary check", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Answer (c): Methods can carry them and is itself over budget, so relocation moved the overrun rather than resolving it. Reallocation is deliberately not decided, because two floors are not enough and Results determines whether there is anything to reallocate."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_namespace_collision", "label": "The A and B id namespaces collided four ways", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fixed structurally only in the files that could still move; this append-only file keeps its old A ids, so anything reading an A-number out of it must check the entry's date and section before mapping it to an approval."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_agentmemory_outage", "label": "agentmemory was not capturing for at least two days", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "With the worker down the MCP tools fall back silently to a flat standalone.json where nothing is indexed for recall. The file store was independently confirmed to carry everything the memories did, which is the check that matters."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_state_store_register", "label": "The state-store register and the sweep that retracted the last entry", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The previous entry recorded four float blockers as open; all four were closed, three before that entry was written. It had been transcribed from a pointer file without checking the files that file points at \u2014 the same failure the entry above it was reporting."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_write_section_hazard", "label": "write_section replaces through to the next same-level heading", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It silently deletes nested subsections; detected by diffing get_sections against the structure recorded before the push. Whole-file write_file is the safer form for a chapter."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_algorithm2e_package_clash", "label": "algorithm + algpseudocode + algorithm2e all loaded", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The [algo2e] option resolves only the environment clash; it does nothing about the command clash on \\For, \\ForEach, \\If, \\ElseIf, \\Return and \\KwTo. Checkpoint A proved the preamble loads and nothing more."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_setkwinout_collision", "label": "\\SetKwInOut declared three times", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It builds its macro with \\newcommand, so the second \\input dies; this can only fire once a document holds two or more algorithm2e floats, which is precisely why the isolated proof harness never caught it."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_static_audit_of_input_graph", "label": "Static audit over the resolved \\input graph", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No tool in the Overleaf bridge can read a compile log \u2014 it is a git clone of the source and Overleaf never commits output.log. The audit found in one pass what two rounds of reading files in context did not, because it ran over the real input graph rather than over the files remembered as pushed."}, {"id": "brain_ledger_phase_state_zotero_false_negative_rule", "label": "A null from zotero_search_by_citation_key is not evidence of absence", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "It scans Extra for a Citation Key line, so it finds only pinned keys; four keys reported not found were confirmed live by title lookup."}], "edges": [{"source": "brain_ledger_phase_state_phase_state_ledger", "target": "brain_ledger_phase_state_prj93_rules", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "brain/ledger/phase_state.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "brain_ledger_phase_state_prj93_rules", "target": "brain_ledger_phase_state_overleaf_gate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTR